F28's silent form (R91b): load decks of sp_mos6 against ngspice-45 with no capacitance, written by ../load.py mos6_nocap.
Builds on PATH: ngspice-45 jfngv2gd3zvi5cmr9vrqfhnziipqd09n (devices/mos6), VACASK dhxz6l3iac3r2b8n91kcz04a0j3hs4s6
(devices/spice/mos6.va, ngspice-47-159 vadng-pre-48). Run: `nix develop .#testing -c tests/fixtures/families/load_run.sh
mos6_nocap` (../../checked.sh). Decks as mos6/ (conditions, regions, readings, probes), the model cards level 6's own
parameters only: no junction or Meyer capacitance (no tox, cgso, cgdo, cgbo, cj, cjsw) and no rd, rs.
Oracles: fd.py (each AC reading against the central differences of the same simulator's DC law) and the m3 relation.
Result: the DC law agrees in every region (3.1e-12 at most). Every ngspice-45 AC deck completes with no
word and prints |i(vd)| = 0 exactly, where its own DC slope is gm 2.9593305e-04 and gds 6.69e-06 (nom_sat) and VACASK
prints its slope (4.3e-10 at most). With rd=10 rs=10 added (internal nodes) the same decks stop with "matrix is singular", as
mos6/ does with the capacitances: the loud form. checked.sh cannot see the silent form (no word, exit 0); the derivative
oracle does. Source: mos6/mos6init.c:43, `.DEVacLoad = NULL`.
Class: F28, an analysis one simulator lacks for a family, here a wrong number with no word.

